"newsgroup" <blah@rogers.com> wrote in message news:<7tj6c.51050$TxJ.28277@news04.bloor.is.net.cable.rogers.com>...
> PDP-11
> 
> I just need to know what it does I am slightly lost :-(
> 
> MOV  R1,  -(R6)
> MOV  R0, R1
> DEC  R0
> BGT  3016
> MOV  R1, R0
> MOV  (R6)+, R1
> RTS  R7
> MUL  #1, R0
> 
> Please let me know if anyone can sorta make out whats going on here?


MOV  R1,  -(R6)   push r1 onto stack
MOV  R0, R1       copy r0 to r1
DEC  R0           subtract one from r0
BGT  3016         branch to location 3016 if r0's contents are greater than zero
MOV  R1, R0       copy r1 to r0, restores r0's contents
MOV  (R6)+, R1    pop stack into r1, restores r1's contents
RTS  R7           return from subroutine using the program counter, r7, for linkage
MUL  #1, R0       multiple r0 by 1

HTH,

Jeff Campbell
