On 2004-03-28, Phillip Helbig---remove CLOTHES to reply <helbig@astro.multiCLOTHESvax.de> wrote:
> I forgot one other question: When one opens up the big door on the
> front, there are three switches.  The top one is for power, the bottom 
> one for reset.  The one between these two is labelled with a triangle 
> inside a circle.  On some VAXstations this is the "HALT" switch.  Is 
> that the case here as well?  If so, why is it a two-position switch like 
> the power switch ("on" and "off") rather than a one-position switch like 
> the reset button which just does something when pressed but doesn't 
> change from one state to another?  Like the power switch, it has a green 
> LED next to it which lights up when it is in the "on" (depressed) 
> position.

On the Alpha, the HALT switch is indeed a two position switch instead of a
momentary one. The switch can be left in when booting to force the system to
stop at the SRM console, independent of the setting of the boot_os or
auto_action variables. Pushing it will also force an immediate drop to the
SRM console.


