>
>Both machines are capable of maximum 4 CPUs, so I tried to put two CPU
>boards into one machine. However, all configs refused to detect more
>than one CPU:

Congrats - you may have the only existing Alphastation 1200a!

Anyway,  you have ev4 and ev45 cpu's in the 1200 and "1200a",
respectively, so they are different chips - not good for SMP.  But, if
you would like to give it a go, try going to the SRM console and
checking "cpus_enabled" for a "3" or higher.  A "1" would be CPU0
enabled, a "3", CPU0 and CPU1.

If you should try to go to ev5 cpu's, it would almost work, but you
would need different firmware to get rid of the solid I/O error toward
the end of the POST.


