gleason@encompasserve.org wrote in message news:<xEPtMhmwcOXJ@eisner.encompasserve.org>...
> Thanks to suggestions on this group, I have been able to read
> and save some old RSX tapes using VMSTPCE (I was surprised when
> I was able to read a BRU tape from 1987, that had been under
> three feet of dirty flood water for two days, that had a nasty
> mudlike crud on it - first pass through the drive knocked all
> the crud off, second pass read the tape, and the output looks fine).
> 
>   I'm using BRUREAD to read the TPC container files, and it's
> working a treat as well.
> 
>   I have a few multi-volume BRU sets here, and I've wondering
> how to deal with them. Any advice on how to read 'em and put
> the individual tapes' containers together?

There is a DECUS tool for VMS, called BRUREAD, that does OK for
reading single-volume BRU tape backups but not so good for multi-volume.

For the "real thing", restore by running BRU under a PDP-11 emulator
against the individual tape images, or run BRU on a VAX in compatibility mode.
Then backup with BRU again.

Tim.


