Thanks; that appears to be an early draft of what I am after
(1972, vs. 1973 for MAINDEC-11-DZQAC-A0), but it may help some.

It is certainly true that most MAINDEC diagnostics were
produced by cross-assembling (usually using "MACY11"),
perhaps on a PDP-10.  I have one listing that shows the
macro package named [400,4531]SYSMAC.C4 and another uses
[400,1066]SYSMAC.SML.  Diagnostic sources themselves
were often named whatever.P11 (presumably indicating
"PDP-11", implying that the host was not a PDP-11).

> or google for "sysmac.sml" and browse further

Unfortunately, essentially all DEC PDP-11 (and maybe other)
OSes include an OS-specific file called SYSMAC.SML, the
contents of which aren't even close to the ones in the
MAINDEC-specific SYSMAC.



