On 2004-03-01, alphadoc <all.the.fun@the.fair> wrote:
> From memory, there is a problem with the firmware onboard. The earlier
> version 2.73?? is detected correctly and works with srm. The later version
> firmware 3.5?? does not.

There are, in reality, two different types of firmware for the DAC960,
corresponding to two different hardware types. One type has one Flash ROM
for firmware, and can only accept firmware versions 2.xx. 2.73 is the latest
version of that firmware. The other has two Flash ROMs, and only uses
firmware versions 3.xx. I don't know what's the latest firmware for those. I
would assume, though, that the ARCFL.EXE utility would be able to update
either to the current version; I know it has 2.73 in it, because that's what
I used to update mine.


