>Is it narrow SCSI on a 68 pin connector?

It is very slow and very narrow ;-)  For some reason, DEC went with this
connector and the rest of the world went for 50-pin Centronics.  (Well,
apart from Apple who decided D25 would do...)

>In either case, I don't have the cable that connects to it.

It's a BC09J or BC56H.  Lots of useful DEC SCSI info at:
http://h18000.www1.hp.com/emea/presalessupport/SCSICableList.html

I have seen people dangling an "internal" cable out the back of a VS3100 to
get around this, such as the one you will find in an external enclosure, IDC
connector one end and Centronics the other.  (A trick also used to get more
devices attached - some VS3100s had two scsi buses.)

